WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:07.040
So now let's see how the database server can execute the CTAs.

00:07.200 --> 00:08.920
So you may ask the data analyst.

00:08.920 --> 00:11.560
You are writing a select into sales.

00:11.560 --> 00:14.160
So that means you are creating a table from a query.

00:14.160 --> 00:19.840
So once you executed the database engine to identify the query first and then execute it.

00:19.840 --> 00:24.840
So it's going to go and select data maybe from the table orders and retrieve the data and return the

00:24.840 --> 00:25.440
results.

00:25.480 --> 00:31.080
Now once the database engine has the results it's going to go and do two things based on the results.

00:31.080 --> 00:32.000
It's going to create.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.520
First a metadata in the system catalog for the table called sales.

00:36.520 --> 00:40.480
And then it's going to go and create a table called sales in the users data.

00:40.480 --> 00:44.360
And this sales table can hold the data from the result of the query.

00:44.360 --> 00:46.560
So it is like any other database table.

00:46.560 --> 00:49.480
It can stores the metadata at the system catalog.

00:49.520 --> 00:53.360
And it can store the data in the disk under the users data.
